**What it does** — reads `{old_id}.note`, parses it with the same `splitn(4, SEP)` used by `load_all`, rebuilds the file with the new id/title while keeping the pinned flag and body verbatim, writes it under `{new_id}.note`, then deletes the old file (skipped if `old_id == new_id`). Tags aren't touched because `load_all` derives them from the body.

